    "case_id": "774",
    "case_summary": "A 54-year-old female with non-insulin-dependent diabetes without standardized hypoglycemic treatment presented with two weeks of fever and chills, followed by sudden onset of confusion and unresponsiveness for half an hour. Two weeks prior, she developed fever up to 37.5°C without other obvious symptoms. On the day of admission, the patient fell while walking and later developed sudden confusion.\n\nPatient showed:- Dull mental state- Slurred speech  - Equal-sized bilateral pupils (3mm diameter)- Sensitive light reflex- Absent breath sounds in right lung- Heart rate: 112 beats per minute- Initial blood pressure: 96/65 mmHg\n\nLaboratory Tests:- C-reactive protein: 197.02 mg/L- Procalcitonin: 10.60 ng/mL- Interleukin-6: 360.4 pg/mL- White blood cell count: 22.88 × 109/L- Neutrophil ratio: 94.6%- Lactate: 6.01 mmol/L- Venous blood glucose: 43.79 mmol/L- Arterial blood gases: pH 7.22- PCO2: 8 mmHg- PaO2: 77 mmHg- HCO3-: 11.6 mmol/LImaging Studies:1. Initial Head CT:   Title: Brain CT on admission   Description: No apparent brain abnormalities2. Initial Chest CT:   Title: Chest CT on admission   Description: Right pneumothorax with consolidation and atelectasis of the right lung3. Initial Abdominal CT:   Title: Abdominal CT on admission   Description: Enormous mixed-density lesions in the liver with fluid gas levels; scattered gas shadows in both kidneys4. Follow-up Head CT (Day 3):   Title: Brain CT on day 3   Description: Right frontal, parietal, and occipital lobes and left parietal and occipital lobes showed infarction with multiple gas accumulations, midline structure shifted left, cerebral herniation presentMicrobiology:- Blood culture: Positive for Klebsiella pneumoniae- Liver puncture fluid culture: Positive for Klebsiella pneumoniae- Pleural drainage culture: Positive for Klebsiella pneumoniae",
